    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look primed for a productive day, anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), who represent our strongest offensive plays. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Littell, and while the opposing catcher's elite pop time marginally tempers his stolen base expectations, his overall profile remains the backbone of today\u2019s production. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a favorable encounter with Canning, where a 14% dynamic platoon boost propels him into the top tier. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** also provide elite floor value; **Gunnar Henderson** overcomes a tough matchup against Miles by leveraging a significant park factor advantage, ensuring his power-speed combination remains locked in the heart of our lineup.\n\nEfficiency optimization forces a difficult decision at the UTIL spot, where **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.95) narrowly missed the \"Strong\" start threshold. While his park factors are excellent, the SP skill of Bradish effectively negates his base projection, making him a risky start in a day where we must manage our game caps carefully. Elsewhere, **Sam Antonacci** (61.66) and **Andy Pages** (64.70) both justify their starts through favorable batting order placement and steady xwOBA metrics, despite the presence of formidable arms like Painter. While we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Drake Baldwin**, our depth remains limited by their ongoing IL stints. We have opted to sit auxiliary pieces like **Heliot Ramos** and **Nolan Schanuel** today, as their current projections fail to surpass the established efficiency of our core group. Keep an eye on **Liam Hicks** and **Brayan Rocchio**; both are hovering near our \"Marginal\" threshold, and should their confirmed lineups shift downward, we may need to pivot to preserve cap space for more favorable matchups later in the week.",
